From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SuperKali <hello@superkali.me>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 21:29:31 +0100
Subject: media: i2c: rk628: fix probe unwind, PLL lock and stream errors

The BT1120 and CSI probes left the subdevice registered, the poll timer
running or the IRQs live on their error paths, and the PLL lock loops
could spin forever. Stream-on reported success without a signal, a
rejected timing change still published new link controls, reset could
leave an IRQ masked across suspend, and the TMDS sample vote compared
only neighbours. Fix those, refuse split CSI output without a second
wired transmitter, report the link rate the TX PHY really programs and
BT.2020 output when the CSC keeps it.

Signed-off-by: SuperKali <hello@superkali.me>
